    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_9",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "A breed group is a categorization of related breeds of animal by an overseer organization, used to organize the showing of animals. In dogs, kennel clubs define the \"Breed Groups\" and decide which dog breeds are to be included in each breed group. The Fédération Cynologique Internationale breed groups are used to organize dogs for international competition. Breed groups often have the names of, and are loosely based on, ancestral dog types of modern dog breeds.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.2227991925571261,
